<h1>US Stone Group — Surfaces Selling &amp; Ordering Guide</h1>
<p class="page-subtitle">Everything you need to quote, sell, and order US Stone Group luxury surfaces through Pinnacle Sales — natural stone, semi-precious, and porcelain.</p>

<h2>The line at a glance</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Natural stone</strong> — quartzite, marble, granite, travertine. Signature lines: Cristallo and Patagonia; plus Taj Mahal, Mont Blanc, Perla Venata, Emerald. 2 cm and 3 cm.</li>
  <li><strong>Semi-precious</strong> — agate, amethyst, crystal quartz, sodalite, decorative mineral slabs. Many translucent / backlight-ready.</li>
  <li><strong>Porcelain</strong> — large-format Italian porcelain in marble, stone, and travertine looks.</li>
  <li><strong>Quarry-direct</strong> — direct relationships with the Cristallo and Patagonia quarry owners; 20-year global sourcing network. Every slab inspected before loading.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How to buy: singles, bundles, and containers</h2>
<p>Pricing is tiered by volume — Singles, Bundles, and full Container quantities, with the container earning the deepest tier.</p>
<ol class="step-list">
  <li><strong>Single slabs &amp; bundles</strong> — for project-by-project selection. Best when a customer needs a specific statement slab or a small run.</li>
  <li><strong>Containers</strong> — for slab yards, fabricators, and dealers stocking inventory. A container is built from one hero material plus a second line to fill the count, at quarry-direct pricing. Public-facing overview: <a href="/playbook/us-stone-container-program">the container program post</a>.</li>
</ol>

<h2>The sales process — five steps</h2>
<p>Consistency protects the customer relationship and ensures accurate pricing, shipping, and fulfillment. When in doubt, get it in writing.</p>
<ol class="step-list">
  <li><strong>Source the material.</strong> Walk the customer through the <a href="/brands/us-stone-group">US Stone Group collection</a> or current inventory. For additional photos, inventory verification, or a FaceTime walk-through of specific bundles, request it through Pinnacle.</li>
  <li><strong>Quote the material.</strong> All pricing comes from the current written price list provided by Pinnacle. No price is final until it's in writing — never quote from verbal communication alone.</li>
  <li><strong>Quote shipping.</strong> Confirm slab count, total square footage, and price per square foot with the customer, then request a shipping quote through Pinnacle using thickness and destination.</li>
  <li><strong>Submit the order.</strong> Send the full customer and material details to Pinnacle Sales. We prepare the sales order, payment instructions, and fulfillment.</li>
  <li><strong>Fulfillment &amp; pickup/delivery.</strong> Buyer arranges transportation and unloading unless otherwise agreed; materials are inspected before they leave the warehouse.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Golden rules</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Quote only from <strong>written pricing</strong> supplied by Pinnacle — never from verbal communication.</li>
  <li>No price is final until it's in writing.</li>
  <li>Always confirm <strong>slab count, total square footage, and price per square foot</strong> before quoting shipping.</li>
  <li>Send every order to Pinnacle with full customer and material details.</li>
  <li>Natural stone varies — color, veining, and texture differences are inherent and not defects. Set that expectation with every customer.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How to get pricing</h2>
<p>The US Stone Group wholesale price list is <strong>confidential</strong> and shared directly with qualified dealers, slab yards, and fabricators — it is not posted here or anywhere on the site. To get the current list, current container availability, or a project quote, contact your Pinnacle rep.</p>

<div class="contact-block">
  <h3>Order &amp; pricing contact — Pinnacle Sales</h3>
  <p>All US Stone Group quotes, pricing, slab photos, inventory checks, and orders route through Pinnacle Sales.</p>
  <p>Submit a request through the <a href="/dealer-hub/submit/?type=surfaces-quote">Dealer Hub request form</a>, or reach your rep directly. We'll handle pricing, shipping quotes, and the sales order from there.</p>
</div>

<h2>Selling tips</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Lead with the hero lines.</strong> Cristallo and Patagonia win projects — they're rare, recognizable, and photograph beautifully. Backlight semi-precious and translucent quartzite for islands and feature walls.</li>
  <li><strong>Finish flexibility closes deals.</strong> Many quartzites can be polished, honed, or leathered — sometimes at no upcharge (confirm per material). Offering the finish choice is a differentiator.</li>
  <li><strong>Bundle the whole project.</strong> You already sell the cabinetry — adding the surface keeps the selection, the margin, and the customer in your showroom.</li>
</ul>

